# Property descriptions → (i) icons

In config builders and designers (`RecordPageBuilder`, `DataTableSettingsDesigner`, `FormBuilder`, etc.):

- Do **not** place long help copy as muted paragraphs under property fields or section titles.
- Put the description on an `(i)` hint button beside the label/title, shown via `v-tooltip` on hover/focus.
- Keep status/preview lines (e.g. “Will show 2 related lists…”, empty-state messages, deprecation warnings) as visible text — those are not property descriptions.
- Match existing hint styling (circular `i` button + tooltip class). Prefer the local pattern already used in the file (`record-page-hint`, `table-settings-hint`, `layout-selector-hint`).
- All hint strings go through `t()`. Use `:aria-label="t('common.moreInfo', 'More information')"`.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<label>{{ t('…', 'Label') }}</label>
<p class="text-muted-color">{{ t('…Hint', 'Long explanation…') }}</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<label class="inline-flex items-center gap-1">
  {{ t('…', 'Label') }}
  <button
    type="button"
    class="record-page-hint"
    v-tooltip.bottom="hintTooltip(t('…Hint', 'Long explanation…'))"
    :aria-label="t('common.moreInfo', 'More information')"
  />
</label>
```
